0..77 Comment "// A path-shaped type takes its carrier by name, as a call takes an implicit."
78..80 Comment "//"
81..157 Comment "// The endpoints often fix the carrier, so a source need not write it first."
158..222 Comment "// A supply by name writes it where the endpoints leave it open."
223..225 Comment "//"
226..301 Comment "// `Path[.A = C](a, b)` supplies the carrier `C`. `Path[.A](a, b)` supplies"
302..372 Comment "// the variable `A` in scope. A universe that a supply names reads the"
373..439 Comment "// endpoints as types. `Bridge` and `Flow` take the same supplies."
440..514 Comment "// `Flow(a, b)` omits its carrier, and the endpoints fix it where the type"
515..524 Comment "// forms."
525..527 Comment "//"
528..614 Comment "// - see: `../../pathological/identity/carrier-by-name.gandr` — the carriers refused"
615..630 Comment "// - see: #4932"
631..705 Comment "// - see: #5026 — a hole in a declared type, solved where the type forms"
